"""
# `_ensure_initialized` must tolerate UNSET logging env vars

Reproduce spec for the defect that blocked every `native-build` on this lane.

`src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/log.spl` imports `env_get` from
`std.nogc_sync_mut.env.variables`, which returns nil / `Option::None` for an
UNSET variable -- unlike `io_runtime.env_get`, which normalizes absent to "".
`_ensure_initialized()` called `.len()` on three such results
(`SIMPLE_LOG_FILE_PATH`, `SIMPLE_LOG_DIR`, `SIMPLE_LOG`) with no guard.

Pre-fix, the first `log_debug` on a process with those variables unset aborts:

    error: semantic: method `len` not found on type `enum`
           (receiver value: Option::None)

Because `_ensure_initialized` runs from the interpreted compiler driver's own
`log_debug` during `parse_all_impl` (step 1 of 6), this killed the build long
before HIR -- measured frame:

    main -> cli_native_build -> compiler_driver_run_compile -> compile
      -> parse_all_committing_impl -> parse_all_impl -> log_debug -> debug
      -> _ensure_initialized

## Honesty note on RED-before

This spec does NOT go RED with the fix reverted -- measured, not assumed:
reverting only `log.spl` and re-running it still reports
`2 total, 2 passed, 0 failed`. Under `simple test` the name `env_get` resolves
to `io_runtime`'s definition, which normalizes an unset variable to "", so the
nil never reaches `.len()`. That is the same collision the compiler warns about:

    warning: public function `env_get` has 4 co-compiled definitions with 2
    differing signatures ((text)->Optional(text) vs (text)->text); JIT call
    sites resolve by exact arg-type match, falling back to the LAST definition
    when types are ambiguous  [compiler_cross_module_private_symbol_collision]

Which definition wins is closure- and load-order-dependent, which is exactly
why the abort appears in the `native-build` worker's closure and not here.

The real RED-before/GREEN-after evidence is the native-build ladder, measured
with a fresh seed on this worktree:

    pre-fix : rc=1, aborts in step 1/6 (parse), `method `len` not found on
              type `enum` (receiver value: Option::None)`, receiver `file_env`
    post-fix: advances to step 2/6 and reaches HIR

This file is therefore a REGRESSION GUARD for the guard's semantics, not a
reproduce. It is kept because it fails loudly if the three normalizations are
removed under any closure where the nil-returning `env_get` wins.

Defect class: unguarded access on an optional whose declared contract says
non-optional. Same class as the two MIR-lowering defects recorded in
doc/08_tracking/bug/simpleos_wm_vulkan_cross_arch_rows_blocked_2026-08-31.md
("Defect 2 -- nil `finally_stack`").
"""

use std.nogc_sync_mut.log.{log_debug, log_info, log_error}
use std.nogc_sync_mut.env.variables.{env_remove}

describe "log._ensure_initialized with unset environment", fn():

    it "does not abort when SIMPLE_LOG_FILE_PATH / SIMPLE_LOG_DIR / SIMPLE_LOG are unset", fn():
        # Clearing all three drives every one of the three previously
        # unguarded `.len()` receivers to nil. Pre-fix this call aborts the
        # whole process; post-fix it returns normally.
        env_remove("SIMPLE_LOG_FILE_PATH")
        env_remove("SIMPLE_LOG_DIR")
        env_remove("SIMPLE_LOG")
        log_debug("reproduce: unset logging environment must not abort")
        expect(true).to_be(true)

    it "keeps the other severities callable with the environment unset", fn():
        # The same lazy-init path is reached from every severity entry point,
        # so a guard applied to only one of them would still leave the build
        # dead on whichever ran first.
        env_remove("SIMPLE_LOG_FILE_PATH")
        env_remove("SIMPLE_LOG_DIR")
        env_remove("SIMPLE_LOG")
        log_info("reproduce: info path")
        log_error("reproduce: error path")
        expect(true).to_be(true)
